  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 246 PM EDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\n- Chance for showers and thunderstorms for some into this evening\n\nWill continue to watch scattered showers and storms work east \nover the next several hours. So far...weather has behaved for much\nof west Michigan though enough instability remains that we could \nsee some storms pop and produce isolated severe/near severe hail \nwinds over the next few hours. Threat near/west of US-131 is over \nfor the day with those east of US-127 and along/south of I-94 \nremaining in the greater risk zone for the next several hours. \nLooks like all storm threat should be out of the area by \n6-7pm...though we could wrap up the potential for storms earlier \nthan that. A few pop up showers will be possible Thursday.\n\n- Warmer next week - occasionally humid and potentially stormy\n\nReturn to hotter, more humid and potentially stormy weather\ncontinues to be the most favored outcome for west Michigan in the\nmid-long range models. 90s at times for highs are not out of the\nquestion at this time with enough moisture and instability for\npotential severe weather on occasion and even heavy rain at times.",
